  "training_signal_warning": "600 development spans carrying 82 uncertain, 61 historical, 47 negated and FIVE family. Five examples cannot teach a class. negated at 47 is also unlikely to beat a checkpoint already fine-tuned on i2b2's thousands.",
  "why": "the gold is frontier-LLM supervision at kappa 0.845-0.913, and an LLM cannot sit in a package that promises replayable edit scripts. An encoder can. This tests whether the supervision transfers.",
  "why_not_the_i2b2_checkpoint": "it beats the rules on negation by 0.117 F1 and covers nothing else. i2b2 assertion has no temporality class, so `historical` has no published baseline anywhere, and the checkpoint dropped associated_with_someone_else as well."
